{
  "title": "Lesson 11. Forms and pseudo-classes",
  "description": "Form tags, label, :hover, :focus, :nth-child",
  "learn": {
    "intro": "Hi! Lesson 11 — **forms and pseudo-classes**. Login, search, comment — they're all forms. We'll make them interactive without JavaScript. Let's go!",
    "sections": [
      {
        "title": "Basic form tags",
        "slides": [
          {
            "emoji": "📝",
            "text": "A form is built from tags:",
            "code": "<form>\n  <input type=\"text\" placeholder=\"Name\">\n  <input type=\"email\" placeholder=\"Email\">\n  <input type=\"password\" placeholder=\"Password\">\n  <textarea placeholder=\"Message\"></textarea>\n  <button type=\"submit\">Send</button>\n</form>"
          },
          {
            "text": "There are also `<input type=\"checkbox\">` (a tick), `<input type=\"radio\">` (pick one) and `<select>` with a list of `<option>`."
          },
          {
            "quote": true,
            "text": "The browser checks `type=\"email\"` itself: if it isn't an email, the form won't send."
          }
        ],
        "check": [
          {
            "type": "choice",
            "topic": "Form tags",
            "prompt": "Which type gives a field that checks for an email?",
            "options": [
              "email",
              "text",
              "mail",
              "check"
            ],
            "answer": 0,
            "explain": "type=\"email\" checks that an email was entered."
          },
          {
            "type": "truefalse",
            "topic": "Form tags",
            "prompt": "<textarea> fits a multi-line message.",
            "answer": true,
            "explain": "textarea is a multi-line field."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "label and for",
        "slides": [
          {
            "emoji": "🏷️",
            "text": "We label the field:",
            "code": "<label for=\"name\">Ваше имя</label>\n<input type=\"text\" id=\"name\">"
          },
          {
            "text": "Why: clicking the label text puts the cursor in the field, and screen readers for visually impaired people read the field correctly."
          },
          {
            "quote": true,
            "text": "The label's `for` must match the input's `id`."
          }
        ],
        "check": [
          {
            "type": "choice",
            "topic": "label",
            "prompt": "What does linking label for=\"name\" and input id=\"name\" give?",
            "options": [
              "Clicking the caption puts the cursor in the field",
              "The field turns red",
              "The form sends itself",
              "The field disappears"
            ],
            "answer": 0,
            "explain": "It is more convenient and accessible."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": ":hover and :focus",
        "slides": [
          {
            "emoji": "🖱️",
            "text": "`:hover` — a style while the cursor is over an element:",
            "code": "button:hover {\n  background: #6d28d9;\n}"
          },
          {
            "text": "`:focus` — a style when the field is selected, i.e. the cursor is inside:",
            "code": "input:focus {\n  border-color: #7c3aed;\n  outline: none;\n}"
          }
        ],
        "check": [
          {
            "type": "match",
            "topic": ":hover and :focus",
            "prompt": "Match the pseudo-class and when it works",
            "pairs": [
              [
                ":hover",
                "The cursor is over the element"
              ],
              [
                ":focus",
                "The field is selected"
              ]
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": ":nth-child, :first-child, :last-child",
        "slides": [
          {
            "emoji": "🔢",
            "text": "`:nth-child()` picks an element by its number among siblings (counting from 1):",
            "code": "li:nth-child(2) { color: red; }      /* 2 */\nli:nth-child(odd) { background: #eee; }  /* 1, 3, 5 */"
          },
          {
            "text": "First and last:",
            "code": "li:first-child { font-weight: bold; }\nli:last-child { border-bottom: none; }"
          },
          {
            "quote": true,
            "text": "Handy for: tables with alternating rows and cards in different colors. Homework: add a subscribe form to your landing from lesson 10."
          }
        ],
        "check": [
          {
            "type": "choice",
            "topic": "nth-child",
            "prompt": "Which of 6 items turn red?",
            "code": "li:nth-child(odd) { color: red; }",
            "options": [
              "1, 3, 5",
              "2, 4, 6",
              "1, 2, 3",
              "3, 4, 5"
            ],
            "answer": 0,
            "explain": "odd means 1, 3, 5."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
